{"uid":"8d053cc223870a91","name":"test_resuming_without_any_ruling_at_all_emits_no_honoured_event","fullName":"tests.test_operator_ruling_reask#test_resuming_without_any_ruling_at_all_emits_no_honoured_event","historyId":"64b8471066896c18703996e2dd38fbf2","time":{"start":1791891719771,"stop":1791891719821,"duration":50},"description":"Task 009 (PRD v0.27 requirement C.2, #274): rewritten from the\n    version that used to pin the pause/re-review/re-park loop C.2 closes\n    -- a bare `resume()` with no ruling filed now records a one-shot\n    'proceed' for this exact rejection's signature, and the SAME rejection\n    reaching `_step_review()` a second time consumes it and takes the\n    ordinary archive-and-replan edge instead of parking a second time (see\n    `tests/test_unpause_one_shot_proceed.py` for the dedicated coverage of\n    that mechanism). This test's own remaining job is unchanged: no\n    ruling was ever filed, so no `operator_ruling_honoured` event fires\n    either way.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 009 (PRD v0.27 requirement C.2, #274): rewritten from the<br />\nversion that used to pin the pause/re-review/re-park loop C.2 closes<br />\n-- a bare <code>resume()</code> with no ruling filed now records a one-shot<br />\n'proceed' for this exact rejection's signature, and the SAME rejection<br />\nreaching <code>_step_review()</code> a second time consumes it and takes the<br />\nordinary archive-and-replan edge instead of parking a second time (see<br />\n<code>tests/test_unpause_one_shot_proceed.py</code> for the dedicated coverage of<br />\nthat mechanism). This test's own remaining job is unchanged: no<br />\nruling was ever filed, so no <code>operator_ruling_honoured</code> event fires<br />\neither way.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791891119430,"stop":1791891119430,"duration